{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'intervals|oauth|refresh_token|expires_in|connect' . --glob '\"'!node_modules/**'\"' --glob '\"'!*.lock'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"./logs/support-tickets.md:1:# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n./logs/support-tickets.md:3:## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n./logs/support-tickets.md:5:> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n./logs/support-tickets.md:6:> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n./logs/support-tickets.md:11:week; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\n./logs/support-tickets.md:14:## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n./logs/support-tickets.md:16:> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n./logs/support-tickets.md:18:> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n./logs/support-tickets.md:19:> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n./logs/support-tickets.md:20:> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n./logs/support-tickets.md:22:Checked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n./logs/support-tickets.md:23:\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n./logs/support-tickets.md:24:`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\n./logs/support-tickets.md:28:Intervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\n./logs/support-tickets.md:30:`connect-attempt.log`).\n./static/app.js:19:    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n./static/app.js:21:    if (st.connected) {\n./static/app.js:22:      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n./static/app.js:24:        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n./static/app.js:26:      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n./static/app.js:27:      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n./static/app.js:28:        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n./static/app.js:32:    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n./static/app.js:33:    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n./config.py:4:APP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n./config.py:6:# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\n./config.py:7:INTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\n./config.py:10:REDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:1:### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:4:2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:5:2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:6:2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:9:    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:18:    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:19:https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:28:    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:32:### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:34:2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:35:2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:37:2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:38:2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:39:2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:40:2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n./logs/connect-attempt.log:41:2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n./README.md:4:plan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\n./README.md:8:\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n./README.md:13:`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\n./README.md:14:while looking into the connection problems.\n./server.py:2:\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n./server.py:13:TOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\n./server.py:14:AUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\n./server.py:22:# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\n./server.py:23:CONNECTIONS = {}\n./server.py:28:    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n./server.py:50:# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\n./server.py:65:def store_connection(user_id, tok):\n./server.py:66:    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n./server.py:67:    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n./server.py:69:        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n./server.py:72:        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n./server.py:74:            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n./server.py:75:            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n./server.py:77:    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n./server.py:80:def refresh_tokens():\n./server.py:86:            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n./server.py:87:                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n./server.py:89:                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n./server.py:90:                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n./server.py:91:                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n./server.py:95:                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n./server.py:99:                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n./server.py:100:                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n./server.py:103:                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n./server.py:104:                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n./server.py:107:def intervals_get(conn, path):\n./server.py:108:    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n./server.py:167:        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n./server.py:169:        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n./server.py:171:        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n./server.py:173:        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n./server.py:179:        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n./server.py:183:                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n./server.py:188:    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n./server.py:197:    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n./server.py:204:            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n./server.py:211:        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n./server.py:218:            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n./server.py:219:        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n./server.py:220:            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n./server.py:221:        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n./server.py:229:            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n./server.py:230:        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n./server.py:231:            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n./server.py:233:            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n./server.py:236:            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n./server.py:242:    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n./server.py:243:    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"В логах видны три связанные проблемы: переход по ссылке теряет заголовок авторизации приложения, URL авторизации содержит повторяющиеся области доступа, а сервер сам помечает выданный токен истёкшим через час. Сейчас сверю это с обработчиками и исправлю поток целиком."}}
